<title>JAPAN: FamilyMart shares up on Walgreen venture.</title>
<headline>FamilyMart shares up on Walgreen venture.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of FamilyMart Co Ltd edged higher on Wednesday, encouraged by news the convenience chain store operator and other Japanese firms had formed a joint venture with Walgreen Co to enter the drugstore business in Japan, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0436 GMT, FamilyMart's shares were up 180 yen at 4,930.</p>
<p>FamilyMart said it and five other Japanese firms -- Itochu Corp, Hac Kimisawa Co, Kraft Inc, CRC Research Institute Inc and Japan Leasing Corp -- had set up a venture with Walgreen capitalised at 250 million yen.</p>
<p>The joint venture company, which will be called RX Network Inc, is expected to have 500 member drugstores in Japan by 2002, a FamilyMart spokesman added.</p>
